  "conclusion": "The nonUSB timebase is independently established, not borrowed from USB. Both images implement the same SysTick formula with different addresses and separate .data source offsets. Shared nominal millisecond arithmetic must not be read as shared physical timing, and USB-specific clock-switch/failure findings must not be projected onto nonUSB.",
